{
	title: 'Local touch crosshair probe for intermittent composer taps',
	spec: 'The web tab menu offers an explicit Touch debug toggle, off on each page load. While enabled, a pointer-events:none overlay marks the latest touchstart coordinates and shows a bounded recent sequence of touchstart/end/cancel, pointerdown/up/cancel, click, focusin/out and visual viewport resize/scroll events, fixed structural target labels, canceled-default state, composer focus, viewport geometry and Send button bounds. Event capture must not prevent default, move focus, submit, or change layout. The overlay captures no input text, names, identifiers or arbitrary attributes and sends/stores nothing. Turning it off removes listeners and overlay; repeated activation does not accumulate them. This diagnoses the invariant that an enabled composer action submits on one deliberate tap without treating an unconfirmed cause as fixed. Web only: the terminal has no browser touch coordinates or software-keyboard viewport.',
